---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import data from '../data/creature.json';

// A census of a private system, published as a frozen snapshot.
//
// Three things were stripped before this shipped: unbuilt work (the roadmap is
// the part worth keeping), file paths and ports (a map of a machine I run), and
// anything that named a person. What is left is what each part does and why it
// earns its place.
const { sections, crypt, diagram, surveyed, counts } = data;

const surveyedLabel = new Date(surveyed + 'T12:00:00Z').toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
  month: 'long',
  day: 'numeric',
  year: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
});
---

<Page
  title="the creature -- anatomy"
  description="A frozen census of a personal agent system: memory that decays, a voice with one permission, and a queue that gates every consequential move. Snapshot, not a product."
>
  <article class="creature">
    <header class="masthead">
      <p class="kicker">a census, frozen</p>
      <h1>The creature</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This is the anatomy of a system I run on one machine, counted on {surveyedLabel}.
        It is frozen at that date and I am not keeping it current. Some of it has
        certainly changed since.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="ground">
      <h2 class="rubric">Read this first</h2>
      <div class="ground-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>What the statuses mean</h3>
          <p>
            <em class="s-live">Live</em> means it runs on a schedule or on demand and I
            would notice within a day if it stopped. <em class="s-part">Partial</em> means
            the core works and something around it does not, and I say which. These are my
            own labels on my own machine. Nobody audited them.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>What is missing on purpose</h3>
          <p>
            Everything unbuilt. The roadmap is the part worth keeping, so it is not here.
            Also every file path, port, and host — this describes a machine I still run.
            You are reading the anatomy, not the address.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>What this is not</h3>
          <p>
            Not a product, not for sale, and not a claim that any of it would survive
            somebody else's hands. One person built it for one person's use. The parts
            worth generalizing are the ones I pulled out into
            <a href="https://github.com/notaprompt/forgeframe">open source</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="ground-note">
        The reason it is on a consulting site: the habits underneath it are the ones I
        bring to client work. Decay instead of infinite storage. One permissioned path
        for anything that speaks. A queue in front of anything that spends. None of those
        were design decisions up front. Every one of them is scar tissue, and you can
        read the wounds — a whole organ exists to stop the system repeating itself,
        because it repeated itself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <figure class="diagram" aria-label="Signal flow from the world through senses, state, mind, memory and dreams, to voice and gated hands">
      <div class="diagram-scroll" set:html={diagram} />
      <figcaption>How a signal travels: in through the senses, into state, through the mind and its memory, out through one voice — and into the hands only after an explicit yes.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    {
      sections.map((section) => (
        <section class="system">
          <div class="sys-head">
            <span class="sys-num">{section.num}</span>
            <h2>{section.title}</h2>
            <p class="sys-gloss">{section.gloss}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="organs">
            {section.organs.map((organ) => (
              <div class="organ">
                <h3>
                  {organ.name}
                  {organ.status === 'partial' && <span class="chip">partial</span>}
                </h3>
                <p class="what">{organ.what}</p>
                {organ.why && <p class="why">{organ.why}</p>}
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </section>
      ))
    }

    <section class="system crypt">
      <div class="sys-head">
        <span class="sys-num">VIII</span>
        <h2>The crypt</h2>
        <p class="sys-gloss">
          What was deleted, and stayed deleted. A census that only lists what survived is
          a sales page.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="tombs">
        {
          crypt.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <span class="tomb-name">{item.name}</span>
              <span class="tomb-what">{item.what}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="tail">
      <p>
        {counts.shown} parts standing, {counts.retired} buried, as of {surveyedLabel}.
      </p>
      <div class="tail-links">
        <a href="/work">What I have built for other people</a>
        <a href="/services">How I work with businesses</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Page>

<style>
  .creature {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  /* ── Masthead ── */
  .masthead {
    border-bottom: 2px dashed var(--white-08);
    padding-bottom: 1.6rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.4rem;
  }
  .kicker {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.24em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold-accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }
  .masthead h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--white-70);
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Ground rules ── */
  .rubric {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--white-30);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .ground {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  .ground-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.6rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .ground-grid h3 {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--glow-hot);
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .ground-grid p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--white-60);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .s-live,
  .s-part {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }
  .s-live {
    color: var(--alive);
  }
  .s-part {
    color: var(--gold-accent);
  }
  .ground-note {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--white-08);
    padding-left: 1rem;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--white-60);
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Diagram ── */
  .diagram {
    margin: 0 0 3.2rem;
  }
  .diagram-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--white-08);
    background: var(--depth-1);
    padding: 1rem;
    color: var(--white-60);
  }
  .diagram-scroll :global(svg) {
    display: block;
    min-width: 620px;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  figcaption {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--white-30);
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  /* ── Systems ── */
  .system {
    margin-bottom: 3.2rem;
  }
  .sys-head {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--white-08);
    padding-bottom: 0.8rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
  }
  .sys-num {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    color: var(--gold-accent);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .sys-head h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .sys-gloss {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--white-45);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  .organs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem 2rem;
  }
  .organ h3 {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--glow-hot);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .chip {
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold-accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--white-15);
    padding: 0.08rem 0.34rem;
  }
  .what {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--white-70);
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .why {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--white-45);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Crypt ── */
  .crypt .sys-num {
    color: var(--white-30);
  }
  .tombs {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .tombs li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 13rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.4rem 1.4rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--white-04);
  }
  .tomb-name {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--white-45);
    text-decoration: line-through;
    text-decoration-color: var(--white-20);
  }
  .tomb-what {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--white-45);
  }

  /* ── Tail ── */
  .tail {
    border-top: 2px dashed var(--white-08);
    padding-top: 1.4rem;
  }
  .tail p {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--white-30);
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .tail-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .tail-links a {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .ground-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.2rem;
    }
    .organs {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .tombs li {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.15rem;
    }
  }
</style>
